// 
// Engine Architecture:
// 
// Application (static)
//  L Application State
//      L IsRunning
//      L Request Close methods
//  L Application Loop ( Launch, Update Loop, Close, Dispose, etc. )
//  L Game
//  L Window Manager
//      L All Windows
//      L Main Window
//      L Active Render Context
//  L Time
// 
// Window
//  L Window Settings
//  L Input
//  L OpenGL Context ( Window ID, Size, Position, State, etc. )
//      L Window Context
//      L Rendering Context
//  L Window Execution ( Open, Update, Display, Close, etc. ) ( DIFFERENT FROM GAME EXECUTION )
//      L Update: Handles Updating this Window
//      L Display: Manages how the Game Context is Displayed ( if at all )
// 
// Game
//  L Game Settings
//  L Game Context ( aka Game Scene ) ( Objects, Drawables, Physics, Cameras, etc. )
//      L Scene Manager
//          L Active Scene
//          L Scene Manipulation Methods ( LoadScene, UpdateScene, DisposeScene, etc. )
//      L PhysicsManager
//  L Game Loop Execution ( Load, Update, Render, Dispose, etc. )
// 
// 
// OpenGL Context Requiring Classes:
//  1. Initialize Settings for creation
//  2. When Used, check for Initialization
//  3. If Not Initialized:
//      - Check for active context
//      - If active context exists:
//          - Initialize
//  4. Continue with action
// 
// Engine Settings Types:
// 
//  Game Settings:
//      Describes how the game should handle certain events (e.g. Physics or Time)
// 
//  Window Settings:
//      Describes a single Window's Context (OpenGL Context, Additional Window Stuff)
// 
//  Application Settings:
//      IDK maybe required so putting it here just in case.
// 